    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379-a1">

                <pb facs="0488" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg380"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 192]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Durham to Mr. Marcelin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am instructed by my last advices from my
                    Government to urge upon your attention the case of Mr. Mevs, and to press for a
                    definite termination of the affair. This legation has for some time past
                    regarded the matter as closed in an amicable <pb facs="0489" n="381"
                        xml:id="pg381"/> way, and the Government of the United States has accepted
                    the settlement. I beg you to give it your early attention, and to advise me when
                    I may look forward to a formal termination.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John S. Durham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
